WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.977
(soft music)

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:25.220
- [Narrator] When you
live in the Swiss Alps,

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:27.500
you have to account for the mountains.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.520
Hence, the cable car.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.890
Life here has forced
residents to get creative

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:33.140
with how they get around.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.600
Here in the cantons of
Obwalden and Nidwalden,

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.470
the cable car tradition dates back to

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:41.253
the beginning of the 20th century.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.280
It's no wonder then that the region boasts

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.830
one of the highest
concentrations of cable cars

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:48.063
in the whole world.

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:51.143
- [Koni] We have small ones,

00:00:51.143 --> 00:00:52.880
big ones and (speaking foreign language).

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:55.950
Then we have also chairlifts.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.290
- [Narrator] Koni here is responsible

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.880
for monitoring an
intricate web of cable cars

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:03.010
that, despite looking new, has been in place

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:04.690
since the 1920s.

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:07.023
It can get riders to vistas like this.

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:10.960
- [Koni] In the morning, we have to start

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:14.480
a cable car down in Engelberg at 6:45.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:16.630
We have to be focused the whole day

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:19.103
to see everything that's happened.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.570
- [Narrator] And while for
some, cable cars are just

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:24.430
a means to reach the mountaintop,

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:27.413
for others, they're private
lifts to their homes.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:35.283
- Hello.

00:01:42.277 --> 00:01:43.340
(Ueli whoops)

00:01:43.340 --> 00:01:46.793
- [Narrator] That's right,
this man has his own cable car.

00:02:03.260 --> 00:02:04.260
His name is Stanton.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:07.023
This champion.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:33.170
- [Narrator] And if you
want to ride in Ueli's

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:36.120
cable car, well, you're
on your own, literally.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:37.913
It's a self-steer operation.

00:02:51.389 --> 00:02:54.972
- My home, Swiss land
mountain farmer here,

00:02:55.978 --> 00:02:57.311
very, very good.

00:03:15.789 --> 00:03:18.289
(theme music)

